(                      _What Is Desirable Weight?_) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Desirable weight is a very individual thing. It may be described as the) Tj T*
(weight at which a person both _looks_ and _feels_ his best. Height, bone) Tj T*
(structure, and muscular development must all be taken into account.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Because no two people are alike, weight tables cannot show with complete) Tj T*
(accuracy exactly what every individual should weigh. The tables shown) Tj T*
(here are given as a guide rather than as a rigid standard to which) Tj T*
(everyone should conform. They show desirable weights for men and women) Tj T*
(at age 25 and over. After a person is full grown and has reached his) Tj T*
(best weight, he should not gain or lose much for the rest of his life.) Tj T*
(It used to be considered inevitable and normal for people to get heavier) Tj T*
(toward middle age. We know now that it is not a normal part of getting) Tj T*
(older, not healthy, and not necessary.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Life is much easier in many ways for people who are not too fat or too) Tj T*
(thin. They usually feel and look better. They are apt to live longer.) Tj T*
(They are less likely to suffer from backaches, foot troubles, constant) Tj T*
(fatigue, and a host of daily discomforts. They have more fun buying) Tj T*
(clothes. Normal weight is worth any effort it takes to reach and) Tj T*
ET
