(social standing, and so eating rich food and too much of it becomes a) Tj T*
(custom. Not infrequently the habit is established in pregnancy, in) Tj T*
(convalescence from some illness, or in other situations when extra food) Tj T*
(may be required.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Other common reasons have their roots in the emotions. Some people eat) Tj T*
(constantly because they are bored, and eating is something pleasant to) Tj T*
(do. Others because they are lonely, or feel unloved, or suffer from) Tj T*
(discontent about money, job, family relationships, or social standing.) Tj T*
(People who overeat for such reasons usually find it necessary to do) Tj T*
(something about their emotional problems before they are able to tackle) Tj T*
(their eating habits successfully.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(_How to Lose Weight_) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Physical condition, degree of overweight, and individual living habits) Tj T*
(must all be carefully evaluated before an effective, safe reducing plan) Tj T*
(can be worked out. No one can do all this for himself. Only a physician) Tj T*
(has the necessary skill and equipment to decide how much, how fast, and) Tj T*
(with what treatment a person should lose weight. What benefits one may) Tj T*
(harm another. Therefore, a reducing program should be undertaken only) Tj T*
(under medical supervision.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Anyone who really wants to get rid of excess poundage can do it. Lots of) Tj T*
(people have, with determination and persistence. Desire and will power) Tj T*
(are ?musts? in any reducing program.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Everyone knows that self-denial is not easy and that changing) Tj T*
(long-established habits taxes the strongest will. Therefore, a person) Tj T*
(who is trying to do this difficult job deserves the help and support of) Tj T*
(his family and friends. Few people are able to persist in any course of) Tj T*
(action in the face of commiseration, indifference, ridicule, or) Tj T*
(opposition from those they love and respect.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(To be worth anything, a loss of weight must be permanent. Therefore,) Tj T*
(anyone who wants to benefit from a weight-reduction program must make up) Tj T*
(his mind that he is changing his eating habits for life. Going back to) Tj T*
(old patterns will only pile up the pounds all over again. Unless this) Tj T*
(fact is accepted, reducing efforts will probably be wasted.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(_The Body?s Need for Food_) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Awake or asleep, the body needs energy for every breath, every) Tj T*
(heartbeat, every activity of living. Food supplies this energy which is) Tj T*
(measured in units called calories.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(When a person eats only enough to supply the energy he uses, his weight) Tj T*
(stays the same. If he takes in more calories than he needs, the excess) Tj T*
(is stored as fat. If his food adds up to fewer calories than he needs,) Tj T*
(his body takes the extra energy out of its storehouse of fat, and a loss) Tj T*
ET
