(in weight occurs. Reducing diets are based on this simple principle:) Tj T*
(_taking in fewer calories than needed to force the body to use its) Tj T*
(stored fat_.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Foods vary in the number of calories they contain. As most people know,) Tj T*
(fats of all kinds have the most calories. One tablespoon of butter, for) Tj T*
(example, has in it about as many calories as a good slice of lean roast) Tj T*
(beef, or a cup of beets, or a quarter of a pound of cod steak. Sugars,) Tj T*
(alcohol, and starches are the next richest source of calories. Starches) Tj T*
(include cereals, flour and everything made with flour, potatoes, peas,) Tj T*
(beans, and corn. When calories must be cut down to make the body use) Tj T*
(stored fat, alcoholic drinks and foods rich in fats, sugars, and) Tj T*
(starches are the first to be restricted.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(However, no one can lose weight safely by counting calories alone. In) Tj T*
(the 1920?s, when a slim, boyish figure was in style, many girls and) Tj T*
(women made themselves seriously ill by reducing their weight without) Tj T*
(regard to the kinds of food they ate.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(For good health, food must supply everyone?young and old alike?with more) Tj T*
(than calories. The body is constantly repairing and renewing itself. New) Tj T*
(cells are always growing to replace those worn out in doing their work.) Tj T*
(In babies, children, and young people, cell-making is going on at top) Tj T*
(speed, because actual growth is taking place. As in any building) Tj T*
(process, the right materials are needed. The body?s most essential) Tj T*
(building and maintenance materials are found in proteins. Foods richest) Tj T*
(in proteins include milk, meat, fish, poultry, eggs, and cheese.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Two other elements necessary for health are vitamins and minerals. Some) Tj T*
(of these are found in the same foods which are rich in protein. Others) Tj T*
(are found in grain products, fruits, vegetables, and fats.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(To insure a well-balanced diet, made up of the protective foods) Tj T*
(containing enough proteins, vitamins, and minerals, everyone should have) Tj T*
(_daily_:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(    _Milk_?2 or more glasses for adults. 4 or more for children and) Tj T*
(          expectant and nursing mothers.) Tj T*
(    _Vegetables_?2 or more servings, green or yellow.) Tj T*
(    _Fruits_?2 servings, 1 a citrus fruit or tomato.) Tj T*
(    _Eggs_?1; at least 3 to 5 a week.) Tj T*
(    _Meat, fish, poultry, or cheese_?1 or more servings \(dried legumes) Tj T*
(          may be substituted occasionally\).) Tj T*
(    _Cereal and Bread_?2 servings, whole-grain or enriched.) Tj T*
(    _Fats_?1 to 3 tablespoons. \(_In reducing diets, some of the fat) Tj T*
(          allowance may be in the cream in whole milk._\)) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(People who are not overweight can add what they like to this list in the) Tj T*
(way of other foods and second helpings, to make up their caloric) Tj T*
(requirements. People who want to lose weight can add little or nothing.) Tj T*
(That is the only real difference between a well-balanced normal diet and) Tj T*
(a well-balanced reducing diet. Because this difference often means) Tj T*
