(_On Keeping a Record_) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Most people find it helpful to keep a record of their progress. Weight) Tj T*
(should be recorded once a week only. To show progress accurately, the) Tj T*
(same scales should be used at the same time of the day.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(It is also helpful to make weekly notes of body measurements. Sometimes) Tj T*
(a person gets discouraged because, after a period of satisfactory loss,) Tj T*
(the scales show no drop for a week or more. But during these periods) Tj T*
(body measurements often continue to decrease. To know that another half) Tj T*
(inch has melted off the waistline is encouraging at such times. It) Tj T*
(stiffens resistance to the common temptation of saying, ?Oh, what?s the) Tj T*
(use?? and stopping when success is in sight. Weight loss begins again if) Tj T*
(the diet is faithfully followed.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The most important record to keep carefully is a list of the foods eaten) Tj T*
(each day, and the quantity. Such a list serves several purposes. It can) Tj T*
(be checked against the essential foods to make sure there are no) Tj T*
(omissions. It will help the doctor in adjusting a diet to slower or) Tj T*
(faster weight loss, as the need may be. It is useful as a reminder of) Tj T*
(slips and indiscretions in eating or drinking which must be checked. It) Tj T*
(helps to keep a person convinced about the number of calories he is) Tj T*
(really taking in.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(_Special Problems_) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(On a reducing diet many people find themselves eating more vegetables,) Tj T*
(raw fruits, and salads than they did before. Most of them benefit from) Tj T*
(the change. However, anyone who has previously had signs of ulcers,) Tj T*
(colitis, or other digestive disturbances should tell his physician. A) Tj T*
(person susceptible to such conditions may need to use raw fruits and) Tj T*
(vegetables sparingly, substituting fruits stewed without sugar, or) Tj T*
(perhaps using pureed vegetables.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Constipation sometimes occurs when eating habits are changed suddenly.) Tj T*
(It can often be corrected by drinking more water and by using green,) Tj T*
(leafy vegetables more generously. The substitution of stewed, dried) Tj T*
(fruits for some fresh fruits may also help. The amount must be watched,) Tj T*
(because dried fruits are richer in calories than fresh fruits. They are) Tj T*
(often eaten in greater quantity and cooked with sugar.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(People who are on a diet and who eat in restaurants a great deal have a) Tj T*
(problem. Unless their budget runs to a daily steak diet, a good) Tj T*
(cafeteria is often a better choice than other types of restaurants. The) Tj T*
(foods are usually plainly cooked, without much fat, and can be chosen) Tj T*
(individually. The chief problem is to develop the habit of passing by) Tj T*
(all the display of foods which must not be eaten. The temptation to add) Tj T*
(something extra is sometimes greater than it is at home.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(If lunch is the only meal which must be eaten out, and there is no) Tj T*
(suitable eating place available, the problem may be solved by taking) Tj T*
ET
endstream
