36 0 obj
<< /Length 2959 >>
stream
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 738 Td 13 TL
() Tj T*
(As in overweight, the first step is to see a physician and have a) Tj T*
(thorough physical examination. It is important to find and correct) Tj T*
(anything which may be wrong. Efforts to gain may be useless unless this) Tj T*
(is done.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The same principles apply to gaining weight as to losing it, but in) Tj T*
(reverse. Underweight people must take in _more_ calories than they use,) Tj T*
(so that there will be some left over to store as fat.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Will power can be as great a factor in gaining weight successfully as it) Tj T*
(is in losing, particularly for people who do not like many of the) Tj T*
(essential foods. They must learn to say ?yes? to enough of the right) Tj T*
(foods, regardless of their wishes, just as firmly as their fat friends) Tj T*
(need to say ?no? to forbidden extras.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(As in overweight, it is important first to include the essential foods) Tj T*
(in the day?s meals. These foods are necessary for maximum health,) Tj T*
(whether a person?s weight is too high, too low, or just right. Some) Tj T*
(underweight individuals whose food choices have been poor may find that) Tj T*
(they are able to gain merely by making sure that they include these) Tj T*
(foods in their diet. Others need to study ways to add extra calories.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(_Adding Extra Calories_) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The simplest way is to eat more at each meal?extra bread and butter, and) Tj T*
(second helpings of everything.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Often, however, underweight people seem to have a small stomach) Tj T*
(capacity. Therefore, additions of high-calorie foods which add little or) Tj T*
(no bulk are probably easier to take at first than trying to eat larger) Tj T*
(quantities. Such additions as cream on cereals and in beverages; extra) Tj T*
(eggs in puddings, salad dressings, and drinks; and butter or other fat) Tj T*
(used generously in salad dressings, cooking and seasoning should add) Tj T*
(enough calories to enable most people to gain weight. Also, provided) Tj T*
(they are added to regular meals and not used to replace them, the) Tj T*
(high-calorie foods listed on page 14 should be used freely by anyone) Tj T*
(trying to gain weight. If they do not interfere with eating enough at) Tj T*
(regular meals, between-meal snacks also help. So do extra milk and) Tj T*
(something to eat before going to bed.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(_Saving Energy_) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The body uses fewer calories at rest than when active, and least of all) Tj T*
(during sleep. Therefore, any extra sleep or rest which an underweight) Tj T*
(person gets will help him to gain. Whatever energy can be saved during) Tj T*
(waking hours by riding instead of walking, sitting instead of standing,) Tj T*
(and relaxing as often as possible will add to the calories saved.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A healthy person who decides to gain weight, and who sticks to his) Tj T*
ET
endstream
